      "usage": "labour, reward, wages, work.",
      "full": "H6468. peullah [ מְּעֻלָּה ] noun feminine work, recompence (in poetry and late); — construct מְּעֻלַּת Lev 19:13 +, suffix מְּעֻלָּתִי Isa 49:4 , etc.; plural construct מְּעֻלּוֺת Psa 17:4 , תֹ - 28:5 ; &#8212; 1 work: a. plural deeds of ׳י Psa 28:5 . b. of men , Psa 17:4 (plural); toil, suffering Jer 31:16 ; good action 2Chr 15:7 , wicked Isa 65:7 , ׳פ שָׁ֑קֶר Prov 11:18 . 2 wages (as earned by work) Lev 19:13 ; Prov 10:16 (|| תְּבוּאָה ), Ezek 29:20 ; reward (from ׳י ) Isa 49:4 ; 61:8 ; probably figurative of people won back by ׳י in warfare 40:10 ; 62:11 (|| שָׂכָר ); of punishment, Psa 109:20 .",
